findings.detail:
_respawn_spot() ranks the ring-1 spots like this:
- in view first;
- then farthest from the player;
- then 'most in front of him'.

With the player on the post, every ring-1 spot is the same distance away. So the tie-break always picks the spot straight ahead, 2 body radii + dummy_respawn_gap_m = 0.8 m from him. That is nearer than any staging distance the bots use (sparring 0.95 m, combos 1.6 m).

In first person the dummy's chest and black guard fists cover more than half the view, and its head is cut off by the top edge. It reads as a body blinking in in his face rather than 'in front of or beside the player, with room'. The waiting itself works: no walk, no push.

